# The Fading Signal
---
Display: The Fading Signal
---
A single scout, a beacon that should be dead, and a long quiet run to whatever
is still transmitting from the edge of the chart.

## Scenario
---
Mode: story
---
// The mission's shape. `Mode: story` = a single-ship narrative with the Admiral
// economy off; no ## Admiralty or ## Worldlets chapter needed. (skirmish / war turn
// on PvP + the RTS; campaign = a persistent solo epic; sandbox = the full universe.)

## Narrative

### A Voice in the Static (signal_1)
---
Scope: shared
State: active
When: reach 3, -2
Then: reveal signal_2
---
Deep-range sensors keep catching the same clipped distress loop from sector
(3, -2) - a Terran registry that went dark eleven years ago. Command wants eyes
on it. Engage the jump drive on Navigation and make the run.

### The Long Quiet (signal_2)
---
Scope: shared
State: secret
When: scan 1 derelict
Pays: 300 credits
---
The signal's source is a cold hulk adrift off the lane - no power, no life, and
a beacon that should have died with its batteries a decade ago. Bring the science
array to bear and find out what is still talking out here.

## Goals

### Answer the Signal (goal_answer)
---
Scope: shared
State: active
When: scan 1 derelict
Win: true
Citation: The beacon's last log finally has a listener. Whatever the Fading Signal was calling into the dark for eleven years, this scout answered it - and flew home with the story.
---
Reach the derelict at (3, -2) and read what its beacon has been repeating into
the static since before you had a commission.

## Landmarks

### The Long Quiet (long_quiet)
---
At: 3, -2
Kind: derelict
---
A Terran survey ship a decade adrift, running lights long cold - and one
stubborn beacon still whispering into the static.
